{"absent":["Locking discipline, interrupt masking, and sleep versus atomic-context rules for these primitives.","Full memory layout of the 32-bit holder and any padding, alignment, or size guarantees beyond the 64-bit counter storage use shown.","Semantics and placement guarantees of the underlying full, acquire, and release fences and ordered single accesses.","Behavior, availability, and side effects of the platform architecture primitives and the set of platforms supplying each ordering flavor.","Progress, fairness, starvation, and bounded-retry guarantees for guarded conditional-store loops under contention.","Interaction with preemption, migration, interrupts, and tearing hazards for nonnative 64-bit access."],"dossier":"D03","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_sub_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_dec_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_inc_and_test"],"text":"The raw layer offers three 32-bit mutating checks that combine an update with a nullness decision: subtracting a caller delta, decrementing by unity, and incrementing by unity each report affirmatively exactly when the stored outcome became zero. Where a platform supplies its own specialized check it is preferred; otherwise the decision follows from the corresponding value-returning update."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative_relaxed"],"text":"The raw layer offers a 32-bit negativity check in four ordering flavors expressing full, acquire, release, and relaxed guarantees. Each flavor adds a caller delta to the stored integer and reports affirmatively exactly when the resulting value is less than zero. Platform specializations are preferred when present, with ordered flavors able to build on the relaxed platform form plus fences or to reuse the full form."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_inc_not_zero","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_inc_unless_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_dec_unless_positive","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_dec_if_positive"],"text":"Guarded 32-bit updates modify the stored integer only under a caller-visible predicate. One primitive skips addition when the observed value equals an excluded sentinel and otherwise adds, reporting the observed predecessor. Related wrappers report success of that conditional addition, increment only nonzero holders, increment only nonnegative holders, decline decrement when the observed holder is positive, and decrement only when the predecessor admits a nonnegative successor while reporting the candidate successor."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_inc_unless_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_dec_unless_positive","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_dec_if_positive"],"text":"Guarded 32-bit modifications follow a shared contention protocol: observe the current holder, test the guard against that observation and leave storage untouched on guard failure, otherwise attempt an atomic conditional store of the computed successor and re-observe on concurrent loss until either the store wins or the guard fails."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_and"],"text":"Plain 64-bit access and update without extra ordering consists of loading the held signed value, storing a supplied signed value, adding a signed delta, subtracting a signed delta, and conjoining a signed mask. These forms delegate directly to the platform layer."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_set_release"],"text":"Ordered 64-bit access consists of a load with acquire guarantees and a store with release guarantees. On one platform branch the operations act directly on the holder storage with single ordered access; on the other branch they pair the plain platform access with the matching fence."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_set_release"],"text":"A 64-bit atomic holder exposes addressable counter storage retaining the signed payload. Ordered access paths name that storage as the object of single ordered load or store on the direct-access platform branch."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_negative_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot"],"text":"Missing ordering flavors are synthesized from available platform flavors under a uniform rule: full ordering combines the relaxed platform form with surrounding full fences, acquire follows the relaxed platform form with an acquire fence, release precedes the relaxed platform form with a release fence, relaxed may reuse the full platform form, and a missing specialized acquire or release may reuse the full form. This pattern applies across negativity, returning-add, fetching-add, returning-subtract, fetching-subtract, unit increment and decrement, and fetching-conjunction families."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_inc_not_zero"],"text":"A 32-bit conditional addition wrapper reports success by comparing the predecessor observation from the fetching conditional addition against the excluded sentinel, and a nonzero-guarded increment reuses that conditional addition with unity delta and zero sentinel."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_andnot","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot"],"text":"Specialized 64-bit unit and mask operations reuse general forms: plain, returning, and fetching increment map to the matching add form with unity delta; plain, returning, and fetching decrement map to the matching subtract form with unity delta; plain mask clearing maps to conjunction with the inverted mask; and fetching mask clearing maps to fetching conjunction with the inverted mask."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_relaxed"],"text":"The 64-bit arithmetic family provides returning and fetching addition plus returning and fetching subtraction, each in full, acquire, release, and relaxed flavors. Returning forms yield the stored successor after applying the signed delta; fetching forms yield the predecessor observed before the update."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_inc_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_dec_relaxed"],"text":"The 64-bit unit family provides plain, returning, and fetching increment plus plain, returning, and fetching decrement, with returning and fetching forms each in full, acquire, release, and relaxed flavors. Returning forms yield the successor after a step of one; fetching forms yield the predecessor; plain forms only update."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_andnot","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot"],"text":"The 64-bit bitwise family provides plain conjunction, fetching conjunction in four ordering flavors, plain clearing, and fetching clearing. Plain forms only update storage; fetching forms yield the predecessor observed before applying the mask or its inversion."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_sub_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_and_relaxed"],"text":"Several 64-bit returning and fetching arithmetic and conjunction operations have no portable emulation in this layer. When a platform supplies neither the full nor the relaxed platform form for the requested operation and ordering, configuring the raw operation fails at build time rather than substituting a generic sequence."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/compiler_types.h::__native_word"],"text":"Ordered 64-bit load and store select between direct ordered storage access and fenced plain access through an external word-size predicate owned elsewhere."}],"index_id":"99dbddb713e8d299bd55ae3ea6f9df9103f2fe09352557dba05a5a735dfe6c48","lane":4,"pass":1,"prefix_sha256":"7e368f1f0746d2b5a4e6bb4196bcc8a374e26ad1af5206ff89af1d2b4c05f323","prompt_sha256":"a5e10ca8688d9ce402516ed8213e191d0e874a4b3d8e94dd2fd612773c66f5